Chapter: DeskCursorArrowTest
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The desktop cursor was a filled rectangle until 2026-08-11 and is now an
 arrow, which means it no longer paints every pixel of the box it reserves.
 That is the whole risk in the change: `cursor-save-rows` and
 `cursor-rest-rows` still save and restore the FULL cwc-by-chc rect, so the
 restore is a superset of what the arrow paints, and a cursor that stopped
 erasing itself would leave a trail of arrows across the desktop rather than
 one cursor.

 It is measured against a framebuffer in memory rather than a display,
 because neither `-mouse` nor `-hid-combo` drives the desk's USB mouse in
 this bed -- both were tried and the cursor stayed where `desk-run` first
 painted it, so no screenshot can show a move.

 The pattern is `i + 1000`, which cannot collide with either cursor colour
 (1052688 and 16777215) at this size, so a pixel differing from the pattern
 is cursor ink and nothing else. Painting 56 pixels twice while only 56 ever
 differ is what proves the erase.

Section: Test

  cur-fb-w : Integer = 32
  cur-fb-h : Integer = 32

  cur-fill : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cur-fill (base) (i) =
    if i >= cur-fb-w * cur-fb-h then 0
    else let w = poke-32 base (i * 4) (i + 1000)
    in cur-fill base (i + 1)

  cur-diff : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cur-diff (base) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= cur-fb-w * cur-fb-h then acc
    else let same = peek-32 base (i * 4) == i + 1000
    in cur-diff base (i + 1) (acc + (if same then 0 else 1))

  cur-alloc : Integer -> Integer
  cur-alloc (size) =
    let raw = __heap-save
    in let adv = __heap-advance (size + 64)
    in (raw + 63) - bit-and (raw + 63) 63

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let base = cur-alloc (cur-fb-w * cur-fb-h * 4)
    in let cs = cur-alloc 2048
    in let p0 = cur-fill base 0
    in let u1 = cursor-update cs base cur-fb-w cur-fb-w cur-fb-h 1 2 2
    in let d1 = cur-diff base 0 0
    in let u2 = cursor-update cs base cur-fb-w cur-fb-w cur-fb-h 1 16 16
    in let d2 = cur-diff base 0 0
    in let hd = cursor-hide cs base cur-fb-w
    in let d3 = cur-diff base 0 0
    in act
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text d1)
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text d2)
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text d3)
    end
  end
